IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgh-address`

-- Tests for sgh-address.l4 (ss 12E and 12F). Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion, before the run.

§ `s 12E: exclusion of the residential address`
-- (test alias a12e1 = `s 12E(1) the Registrar must cause the residential address to be excluded from public access`)
-- arguments: a director's, chief executive officer's or secretary's address in a register under section 173(1); an individual member's address in the register kept under section 196A of a private company
#ASSERT `s 12E(1) the Registrar must cause the residential address to be excluded from public access` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the residential address of a director, chief executive officer or secretary of a company contained in the register of directors, register of chief executive officers or register of secretaries"
#ASSERT `s 12E(1) the Registrar must cause the residential address to be excluded from public access` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the residential address of a member of a private company, who is an individual, contained in the electronic register of members"
#ASSERT `s 12E(1) the Registrar must cause the residential address to be excluded from public access` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an address of another kind: the text says nothing (limited by its own wording)
-- (test alias a12e2 = `s 12E(2) the Registrar may cause the residential address to cease to be excluded from public access`)
-- arguments: the address is excluded under section 12(2)(c) or (d) pursuant to (1) or (3); the Registrar has proceeded in accordance with section 12F
#ASSERT `s 12E(2) the Registrar may cause the residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Where, pursuant to subsection (1) or (3), the residential address ... is excluded from public access ..., the Registrar may cause the residential address to cease to be excluded ... in accordance with section 12F"
#ASSERT `s 12E(2) the Registrar may cause the residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- excluded, but the Registrar has not followed section 12F: the text says nothing of an exercise "in accordance with section 12F" that is not (grant ruling, limit 1)
#ASSERT `s 12E(2) the Registrar may cause the residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the address is not so excluded: a failed "Where" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
#ASSERT `s 12E(2) the Registrar may cause the residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not so excluded and section 12F not followed: the failed "Where" decides first
-- (test alias a12e3 = `s 12E(3) the Registrar must cause the exclusion from public access to resume`)
-- arguments: the address has ceased to be excluded pursuant to (2); notice of a change of contact address lodged; section 12F(8) bars the lodging; the Court directed resumption on an appeal under 12F(7)
#ASSERT `s 12E(3) the Registrar must cause the exclusion from public access to resume` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) subject to section 12F(8) ..., notice of a change in the individual's contact address is lodged"
#ASSERT `s 12E(3) the Registrar must cause the exclusion from public access to resume` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) the Court so directs on an appeal under section 12F(7)"
#ASSERT `s 12E(3) the Registrar must cause the exclusion from public access to resume` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "subject to section 12F(8)": the lodging is barred, and the Court gave no direction
#ASSERT `s 12E(3) the Registrar must cause the exclusion from public access to resume` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- barred under (a), but "(b) the Court so directs" stands alone
#ASSERT `s 12E(3) the Registrar must cause the exclusion from public access to resume` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither limb of the "if": the duty does not arise
#ASSERT `s 12E(3) the Registrar must cause the exclusion from public access to resume` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the address has not ceased to be excluded: a failed "Where"
-- (test alias a12e4 = `s 12E(4) the Registrar must cause the residential address to be excluded from public access in respect of the document`)
-- arguments: filed or lodged by a form on the electronic transaction system on or after the commencement of section 30 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024; an individual's residential address is entered in the form
#ASSERT `s 12E(4) the Registrar must cause the residential address to be excluded from public access in respect of the document` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) a document is filed or lodged with the Registrar ... by submitting a form on the electronic transaction system on or after the date of commencement ...; and (b) an individual's residential address is entered in that form"
#ASSERT `s 12E(4) the Registrar must cause the residential address to be excluded from public access in respect of the document` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "(b)" unmet: a failed "Where"
#ASSERT `s 12E(4) the Registrar must cause the residential address to be excluded from public access in respect of the document` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "(a)" unmet: a failed "Where"

§ `s 12F: ending the exclusion`
-- (test alias a12f1 = `s 12F(1) a ground exists for causing the residential address to cease to be excluded from public access`)
#ASSERT `s 12F(1) a ground exists for causing the residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) communications sent by the Registrar ... to the individual at the contact address and requiring a response within a specified period remain unanswered"
#ASSERT `s 12F(1) a ground exists for causing the residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) there is evidence to show that service of a document ... at the individual's contact address is not effective to bring it to the notice of the individual"
#ASSERT `s 12F(1) a ground exists for causing the residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- both grounds
#ASSERT `s 12F(1) a ground exists for causing the residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "the grounds ... are either that (a) ... or (b)": a closed list
-- (test alias a12f2 = `s 12F(2) the Registrar must give the person the notice under subsection (3) before causing the residential address to cease to be excluded`)
-- arguments: the Registrar is about to cause the cessation pursuant to 12E(2); the person is the individual; the person is a company the Registrar was notified of as having the individual as director, CEO or secretary; the person is a private company the Registrar was notified of as having the individual as member
#ASSERT `s 12F(2) the Registrar must give the person the notice under subsection (3) before causing the residential address to cease to be excluded` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) the individual"
#ASSERT `s 12F(2) the Registrar must give the person the notice under subsection (3) before causing the residential address to cease to be excluded` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) every company of which the Registrar has been notified under this Act that the individual is a director, chief executive officer or secretary"
#ASSERT `s 12F(2) the Registrar must give the person the notice under subsection (3) before causing the residential address to cease to be excluded` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(c) every private company of which the Registrar has been notified ... that the individual is a member"
#ASSERT `s 12F(2) the Registrar must give the person the notice under subsection (3) before causing the residential address to cease to be excluded` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- anyone else: the text says nothing of any further recipient
#ASSERT `s 12F(2) the Registrar must give the person the notice under subsection (3) before causing the residential address to cease to be excluded` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the Registrar is not about to do so: the duty is gated by "Before causing"
-- (test alias a12f3 = `s 12F(3) the notice has the content the subsection requires`)
#ASSERT `s 12F(3) the notice has the content the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) state the grounds under subsection (1) ...; and (b) specify the period within which representations may be made"
#ASSERT `s 12F(3) the notice has the content the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no period for representations specified: the content duty is not met
#ASSERT `s 12F(3) the notice has the content the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- grounds not stated: the content duty is not met
-- (test alias a12f4 = `s 12F(4) the Registrar must consider the representation`)
-- arguments: given in response to the notice; the date received; the last day of the period the Registrar specified
#ASSERT `s 12F(4) the Registrar must consider the representation` TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the representations (if any) given in response to the notice ... received within the period specified by the Registrar"
#ASSERT `s 12F(4) the Registrar must consider the representation` TRUE (Date 31 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- received on the last day of the period: within it
#ASSERT `s 12F(4) the Registrar must consider the representation` TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day late: a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `s 12F(4) the Registrar must consider the representation` FALSE (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in response to the notice mentioned in (2): the text says nothing (limited by its own wording)
-- (test alias a12f5 = `s 12F(5) the Registrar must give the person notice of the decision before doing so`)
-- arguments: the Registrar decides to cause the cessation; the person is the individual; the person is a company mentioned in (2)(b) or (c)
#ASSERT `s 12F(5) the Registrar must give the person notice of the decision before doing so` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) the individual"
#ASSERT `s 12F(5) the Registrar must give the person notice of the decision before doing so` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) every company mentioned in subsection (2)(b) and (c)"
#ASSERT `s 12F(5) the Registrar must give the person notice of the decision before doing so` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- anyone else: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 12F(5) the Registrar must give the person notice of the decision before doing so` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no decision to cause the cessation: a failed "If"
-- (test alias a12f6a = `s 12F(6) the notice to the individual must be sent to the individual's residential address`)
#ASSERT `s 12F(6) the notice to the individual must be sent to the individual's residential address` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "must be sent to the individual's residential address"
#ASSERT `s 12F(6) the notice to the individual must be sent to the individual's residential address` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless it appears to the Registrar that service at that address may be ineffective to bring it to the individual's notice"
-- (test alias a12f6b = `s 12F(6) the notice may be sent to another last known address of the individual`)
#ASSERT `s 12F(6) the notice may be sent to another last known address of the individual` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "in which case it may be sent to any other last known address of that individual"
#ASSERT `s 12F(6) the notice may be sent to another last known address of the individual` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- service at the residential address does not appear ineffective: the text says nothing of another address (the first limb governs)
-- (test alias a12f7 = `s 12F(7) the individual may appeal to the Court against the decision`)
-- arguments: aggrieved by the decision under 12E(2); the date the notice under (5) was received; the date the appeal is brought
#ASSERT `s 12F(7) the individual may appeal to the Court against the decision` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "within 30 days after the date of receiving the notice": 1 March plus 30 days is 31 March, the last day in time
#ASSERT `s 12F(7) the individual may appeal to the Court against the decision` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the day of receipt is in time (fork line F-H-P2)
#ASSERT `s 12F(7) the individual may appeal to the Court against the decision` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day late: a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `s 12F(7) the individual may appeal to the Court against the decision` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before the notice was received: no appeal yet lies
#ASSERT `s 12F(7) the individual may appeal to the Court against the decision` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not aggrieved: the right is "Any individual aggrieved by the decision" (limited by its own wording)
-- (test alias a12f7c = `s 12F(7) the Court may confirm or reverse the decision of the Registrar and make any directions in the matter`)
#ASSERT `s 12F(7) the Court may confirm or reverse the decision of the Registrar and make any directions in the matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the Court may confirm or reverse the decision of the Registrar and make such directions in the matter as it thinks fit"
#ASSERT `s 12F(7) the Court may confirm or reverse the decision of the Registrar and make any directions in the matter` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no appeal brought within the period: the text says nothing of the Court's power outside an appeal
-- (test alias a12f8 = `s 12F(8) the individual is barred from providing a contact address`)
-- arguments: the date the Registrar caused the cessation; the date the individual provides a contact address; good cause satisfied
#ASSERT `s 12F(8) the individual is barred from providing a contact address` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "within 3 years after": the day of the cessation is inside the period (fork line F-H-P2)
#ASSERT `s 12F(8) the individual is barred from providing a contact address` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2029) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last day of the 3 years: 10 January 2026 plus 3 years is 10 January 2029
#ASSERT `s 12F(8) the individual is barred from providing a contact address` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 11 1 2029) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day after the 3 years: a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `s 12F(8) the individual is barred from providing a contact address` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 9 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before the cessation: the 3 years have not begun
#ASSERT `s 12F(8) the individual is barred from providing a contact address` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 6 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the Registrar is satisfied that there is good cause": inside the 3 years, good cause shown
#ASSERT `s 12F(8) the individual is barred from providing a contact address` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 6 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- inside the 3 years, no good cause: barred
-- (test alias a12f9 = `s 12F(9) the Registrar must replace the individual's contact address in each register kept under section 12(1) with the new contact address`)
-- arguments: the individual provides a new contact address under an ACRA administered Act; subsection (8) bars the individual from providing it
#ASSERT `s 12F(9) the Registrar must replace the individual's contact address in each register kept under section 12(1) with the new contact address` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Where an individual provides a new contact address under any ACRA administered Act, the Registrar must replace the individual's contact address in each register kept under section 12(1)"
#ASSERT `s 12F(9) the Registrar must replace the individual's contact address in each register kept under section 12(1) with the new contact address` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Subject to subsection (8)": barred, so no replacement is owed
#ASSERT `s 12F(9) the Registrar must replace the individual's contact address in each register kept under section 12(1) with the new contact address` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no new contact address provided: a failed "where"

§ `Regulative rules of ss 12E and 12F: no time limit and no consequence the text states, so no breach path`
-- With no deadline, a late act still reads FULFILLED and no act reads RESIDUAL; the rules appear in "Rules with no breach path" in NOTES.md.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 12E(1) rule: the Registrar's duty to exclude the residential address from public access` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 12E(1) cause the residential address to be excluded from public access` AT 900
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 12E(1) rule: the Registrar's duty to exclude the residential address from public access` 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 12E(3) rule: the Registrar's duty to cause the exclusion to resume` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 12E(3) cause the exclusion from public access to resume` AT 8
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 12E(3) rule: the Registrar's duty to cause the exclusion to resume` 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 12E(4) rule: the Registrar's duty to exclude the residential address entered in the form` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 12E(4) cause the residential address to be excluded from public access in respect of the document` AT 3
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 12E(4) rule: the Registrar's duty to exclude the residential address entered in the form` 7 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 12F(2) rule: the Registrar's duty to give the notice under subsection (3)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 12F(2) give the individual, and each company the paragraphs name, the notice under subsection (3)` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 12F(2) rule: the Registrar's duty to give the notice under subsection (3)` AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 12F(4) rule: the Registrar's duty to consider the representations` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 12F(4) consider the representations given in response to the notice` AT 6
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 12F(4) rule: the Registrar's duty to consider the representations` AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 12F(5) rule: the Registrar's duty to give notice of the decision` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 12F(5) give notice of the decision to the individual and to each company` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 12F(5) rule: the Registrar's duty to give notice of the decision` AT 0 WITH
-- The bar of s 12F(8): the number of days in the 3 years is an input (1,095 or 1,096, by the leap days they hold; 1,096 is used here). The individual provides a contact address on day 400: the prohibition is violated.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 12F(8) rule: the individual's bar on providing a contact address` "Lee" 1096 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Lee" DOES `s 12F(8) provide a contact address` AT 400
-- The 1,096 days pass and the individual has provided nothing: the prohibition was respected.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 12F(8) rule: the individual's bar on providing a contact address` "Lee" 1096 AT 0 WITH
    (`WAITUNTIL` 1097)
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 12F(8) rule: the individual's bar on providing a contact address` "Lee" 1096 AT 0 WITH
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 12F(9) rule: the Registrar's duty to replace the contact address` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 12F(9) replace the individual's contact address in each register kept under section 12(1)` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 12F(9) rule: the Registrar's duty to replace the contact address` 7 AT 0 WITH
